  "id": "983069784",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "Ecclesiasterion (Odeion) at Messene",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/odeon"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Construction of the Ecclesiasterion (or Odeion) at Messene is believed to have started in the third century BCE, and it was repaired in the first and third century CE. The structure may have originally been an ecclesiasterion or bouleuterion before being converted into an odeon. It is part of the architectural complex of the Asklepieion of Messene, and is fully excavated and visitable today.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Ecclesiasterion (Odeion) at Messene was originally constructed in the third century BCE and may be a converted ecclesiasterio/bouleuterion.",
